<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 2.346 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 2.346 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 2.346 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers added the central bank had offered a combination of three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>    150 million    363 days</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     42 days</p>
<p>    400 million     19 days</p>
<p>    700 million     13 days</p>
<p>    296 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
